  Derived (surface extraction, smoothing, decimation, quantization) from the TotalSegmentator
  v2 dataset (small subset v2.0.1, subject s1369), licensed CC BY 4.0.
  Wasserthal J, et al. TotalSegmentator: Robust Segmentation of 104 Anatomic Structures in
  CT Images. Radiol Artif Intell. 2023. https://doi.org/10.1148/ryai.230024
  Dataset: https://zenodo.org/records/10047263 — https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
  The derived atlas is distributed under CC BY 4.0.

Lower-limb atlas (32 structures, src/data/lower_limb_atlas.js)
  Derived from BodyParts3D version 4.0 (PART-OF tree), © The Database Center for Life
  Science (DBCLS). Mitsuhashi N, et al. BodyParts3D: 3D structure database for anatomical
  concepts. Nucleic Acids Res. 2009;37:D782-5.
  https://dbarchive.biosciencedbc.jp/en/bodyparts3d/
  Licence note: the current archive page states CC BY 4.0, while the OBJ file headers carry
  the legacy CC BY-SA 2.1 Japan licence. To respect both, the derived lower-limb atlas is
  distributed under CC BY-SA 2.1 Japan (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.1/jp/)
  with the attribution above; this share-alike term applies to that data file, not to the
  application code.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Neural landmark model — NOT included in this repository
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The optional neural AP engine uses the network architecture of:
  Yi J, Wu P, Huang Q, Qu H, Metaxas DN. Vertebra-Focused Landmark Detection for Scoliosis
  Assessment. ISBI 2020. Code: https://github.com/yijingru/Vertebra-Landmark-Detection (MIT).
The authors' trained weights were published without a licence statement and were trained on
the AASCE 2019 / SpineWeb dataset 16, whose terms could not be verified. The weights
(ai-tools/assets/weights.b64) are therefore NOT distributed here, and public builds are made
without them. ai-tools/assets/model_topology.json describes the converted graph (no weights);
ai-tools/assets/spec.json holds reference outputs on a synthetic test pattern used by the
self-test.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Literature-derived parameters
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Procedure correction defaults and bounds, classification thresholds (SRS-Schwab), age-adjusted
reference values (Lafage R, et al. Spine 2016) and gait cohort couplings (North American Spine
Society Journal cohort data) are cited at their point of use in src/js/app/01-data.js and shown
in the application. They are facts and published values, used with citation.
